# Grammar for the sofiia-grounded-json-v0.1 contract.
#
# The system prompt asks for this shape in prose and the model does not
# reliably obey it. OLMo 2 7B returned an object whose answer string continued
# "Citations:" and inlined citation objects as text; OLMo 2 1B nested the whole
# schema inside the answer string with unescaped quotes. Neither is a prompting
# problem, and the bounded correction cannot recover output that never parses.
#
# response_format {"type":"json_object"} is accepted by llama-server and is NOT
# enforced on this build: measured against the running server, output was
# byte-identical with and without it, markdown code fence included. A GBNF
# grammar IS enforced, so this file is what actually holds the shape.
#
# Every rule must sit on ONE line. llama.cpp's GBNF parser ends a rule at the
# newline, so a rule body wrapped across lines is a parse error - which reads
# only as "failed to parse grammar" and took a bisect to find.
#
# v0.2 bounds the answer string. A 7B model asked this question wrote past the
# token limit and the object was cut off mid-sentence, so a draft that was on
# its way to being correct was rejected for length alone. The prompt asks for
# 120 words and the prompt is not binding; this is. The bound is generous -
# roughly 900 characters, comfortably more than 120 words - because it exists
# to stop a runaway, not to shape the prose.
#
# string and ws are llama.cpp's own rules from grammars/json.gbnf, so escaping
# behaves exactly as its JSON grammar does. Key order is fixed: it costs the
# model nothing and removes permutations a small model spends tokens getting
# wrong. The grammar guarantees shape, never truth - whether a citation names
# a real segment and whether a quote appears in its source is the verifier's
# job, and stays the verifier's job.

root ::= "{" ws "\"answer\":" ws answerstring "," ws "\"citations\":" ws idarray "," ws "\"quotes\":" ws quotes "," ws "\"abstain\":" ws boolean "}" ws
idarray ::= "[" ws ( string ("," ws string)* )? "]" ws
quotes ::= "[" ws ( qitem ("," ws qitem)* )? "]" ws
qitem ::= "{" ws "\"segment_id\":" ws string "," ws "\"text\":" ws string "}" ws
boolean ::= ("true" | "false") ws
string ::= "\"" ( [^"\\\x7F\x00-\x1F] | "\\" (["\\bfnrt] | "u" [0-9a-fA-F]{4}) )* "\"" ws
answerstring ::= "\"" ( [^"\\\x7F\x00-\x1F] | "\\" (["\\bfnrt] | "u" [0-9a-fA-F]{4}) ){1,900} "\"" ws
ws ::= | " " | "\n" [ \t]{0,20}
